  "body": "Implements #3984 (design `doc/2026-11-01T21-07-00Z_design_pm-stack_forecasting.md` §4, parent chain #1184 → #1256): one machine-first forecast contract that Roadmap and Projects consume identically.\n\n## What lands\n\n- **`src/forecast-contract.ts`** — the shared contract (`forecast-contract/v1`). Three separate forecast types, so missing data in one plane never makes another look more certain:\n  - `epic_completion` — wraps `deriveEpicEta` (#3982): scope/subject, `asOf`, model version, input window/coverage, remaining units, nullable P50/P80, confidence (evidence grade), baseline source, structured `reasons`/`limitations`. GitHub-vs-Project status disagreement is surfaced as a structured reason, never resolved silently.\n  - `quota_exhaustion` — per-pool wall interval from a measured burn rate in the pool's own units, with next reset, remaining/limit, and before/after-reset disposition. The per-pool rate-history model is #3983 (still open); absent/stale/zero rate ⇒ the first-class `quota_rate_unavailable` / `no_recent_burn` states — no invented date, never \"safe\". A single linear rate collapses the interval to the point estimate and says so in `limitations`.\n  - `stall_risk` — wraps `deriveStallRisk` (§3): score + threshold + contributing signals; unknown signals are named limitations; `escalatesToNeedsYou` stays `false`.\n  - `formatForecastSummary` — the one-line rendering both pages share: range (or named no-date state) + confidence + input summary together. Never a bare date; missing values never render as zero.\n- **`GET /api/forecasts.json`** — serves the identical contract objects (`?subject=` filters). Epic/stall subjects derive from the stored item history (#3981, new `cfg.itemHistoryFile` / `PM_AGG_ITEM_HISTORY_FILE`, default state-dir `item-history.jsonl`); quota contracts build from the live quota view (token burn rate only when the window unit is tokens and gatherer freshness is ok).\n- **Rendering** — Roadmap drill-down (matched epic) and Projects pool cards render the same summaries via optional `forecasts` maps threaded through `renderRoadmap` / `projectsBodyHtml` / `renderProgram`; absent forecasts render exactly as before.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test/forecast-contract-3984.test.ts` (16 tests, named oracle = design §4): high/low (borrowed baseline)/unavailable confidence, stale source, missing baseline/limit/reset, all three forecast types, plus Roadmap + Projects rendering of the same contract. Full aggregator suite: 1830 pass / 18 fail — identical 18 failures on a clean-main baseline worktree (1814 pass / 18 fail), so no regressions; `tsc --noEmit` clean on touched files.\n\nQueue: task 14323 (replacement for task 12141), lane code-k, execution lane direct.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796828364&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8051&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8051&signature=494efd8ace4ffc672f230d934d50f6e5b4ad065afac75646c2ecfe8785119d13\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8051?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
